Exported symbol: FIO_createFilename_fromOutDir — confirmed via nm -D

Key translation decisions:
- Used extern "C" FFI to call calloc, strlen, strrchr, memcpy, fprintf, strerror, exit directly — this guarantees byte-identical output since we're using the exact same libc functions the C code uses
- extractFilename is kept as an internal (non-exported) helper
- The #ifdef _MSC_VER / __MINGW32__ Windows branches are dead code on Linux, so the separator is always '/'
- The error path (fprintf(stderr, "zstd: FIO_createFilename_fromOutDir: %s", strerror(errno)); exit(30)) is preserved exactly, including the format string without a trailing newline (matching the original C bug)
- errno is read via __errno_location() on Linux / __error() on macOS
